From 55bde6ae539076b351a03a60a011d4a2bf307cdf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 13:43:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] AiMesh backhaul parking: reconcile against the live carrier
 state every tick

A wireless restart - a Network or Wireless page apply, an SDN change, the
mesh daemon's own rebuilds - re-creates every BSS, so a carrier the daemon
had parked came back on the air while its record still said parked, and
the park pass skipped it for ever. Only switching parking off and on
cleared the record (owner, 2026-09-06, v3.1.0).

The daemon now forgets a claim whose carrier reads "up", logs why, and
parks it again on the same tick. Covers every source of a restart at once
instead of hooking one entry point.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src/router/rc/amaspark.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/release/src/router/rc/amaspark.c b/release/src/router/rc/amaspark.c
index 2aa87ae8d5..f5b9cc8c07 100644
--- a/release/src/router/rc/amaspark.c
+++ b/release/src/router/rc/amaspark.c
@@ -230,6 +230,18 @@ int amaspark_main(int argc, char *argv[])
 
 		if (want) {
 			int acted = 0;
+			/* reaper v3.1.0 (owner 2026-09-06): a wireless restart - a Network or
+			 * Wireless page apply, an SDN change, cfg_server's own rebuilds -
+			 * re-creates every BSS, so a carrier we parked is back on the air
+			 * while our record still says parked, and the loop below would skip
+			 * it for ever. Reconcile against the live state every tick: forget
+			 * the stale claim, say so, and let the pass below park it again. */
+			for (u = 0; u < AP_MAXU; u++) {
+				if (!parked[u] || !ifn[u][0] || before[u] != 1) continue;
+				parked[u] = 0;
+				changed = 1;
+				logmessage(AP_TAG, "%s (%s backhaul carrier) came back up - a wireless restart re-created it; parking it again", ifn[u], band_name(nband[u]));
+			}
 			for (u = 0; u < AP_MAXU; u++) {
 				if (!ifn[u][0] || !radio[u] || parked[u]) continue;
 				if (nband[u] == 4) continue;		/* 6 GHz: never by our hand */
